th a gap + a failed form | counts, last position, gaps, failed derivations all visible |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:38:- Productionized converter from PI `message_end` and runtime-selection hooks to LHC `MessageEventInput` events.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:58:**AC-2.1:** Every PI message finalized through `message_end` — user, assistant, tool result — is mapped to LHC intake events and recorded in source order. An assistant message fans out to per-content-part events in thinking → text → tool-call order: `assistant_thinking`, `assistant_text`, and one `tool_call` per call.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:62:**AC-2.2:** LHC turn boundaries are derived from PI traffic, not from PI's per-agent-step `turn_end`. One LHC turn spans a user prompt and all subsequent agent activity until the next user prompt or the end of the agent run. The converter emits exactly one LHC `turn_end` event per LHC turn, at the agent run's completion — never one per PI `turn_end`, and never keyed off PI's per-agent-run `turnIndex` as a session counter.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:66:**TC-2.3** — Session order derives from converter source-event order, not `turnIndex`; two agent runs each starting at `turnIndex 0` order correctly.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:76:**AC-2.5:** A graceful interrupt — a complete turn PI marks aborted, with partial assistant content preserved — is captured whole: the partial content is recorded and the aborted disposition is carried through. The interrupted content is 