rompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:328:| TC-6.3 | inspect overview/health reflect captured session | a captured thread with a gap + a failed form | counts, last position, gaps, failed derivations all visible |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:475:        evidence: \"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:493:        evidence: \"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:585:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) — Chunk 2 — TDD Red→Green. Red: wrote 5 capture test files driving the production hook→converter→real-LHC-intake path plus direct unit calls, confirmed all 21 fail for the right reason against the fail-closed skeletons (never asserting on NotImplementedError), and froze them in red-manifest.json. Green: implemented idempotency.eventKey (precedence entryId→toolCallId→responseId→content-fingerprint), the pure map-message (assistant fan-out thinking→text→tool_call, tool_result correlation by toolCallId with error flag, unsupported parts and empty messages degrade to runtime_note, graceful-interrupt disposition carried on a trailing runtime_note), the TurnAccumulator (open-turn tracking; exactly one turn_end at agent_end; replay-stable turn keys; hard-kill leaves the turn open), runtime-changes (model_select/thinking_level_select → ordered runtime_notes carrying new+previous), and converter.capture (failure isolation: invalid_event on a writable thread records a durable gap runtime_note; store-unavailable surfaces as a structured error, never a throw). Wired index.ts message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end to the converter with per-session capture state (open-turn accumulator + monotonic source-event index) and mapped failures into SessionState.health; PI per-step turn_end stays a no-op (ignored as an LHC boundary).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:592:        reason: \"Implemented the pure mapper: user→user_prompt, assistant fan-out (thinking→text→tool_call), tool_result correlated by toolCallId with an always-set isError flag, unsupported parts and wholly-empty messages → runtime_note (never a silent drop), and the aborted-disposition runtime_note; exported ABORTED_DISPOSITION_TEXT for fixture lock-step.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:604:        reason: \"Wired the capture hook rail (message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end) through map→accumulate→converter into real LHC intake; added per-session capture state (accumulator + source-event index) in the closure; mapped capture failures into SessionState.health (recordedGap true on invalid_event, false on store-unavailable); turn_end remains a no-op.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:610:        reason: \"NEW — TC-2.2 worked example (one turn_end at agent_end), TC-2.3 source-order-not-turnIndex, accumulator state-machine goldens, hard-kill golden.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:616:        reason: \"NEW — TC-2.6 graceful interrupt: partial content preserved, aborted disposition carried, turn closes complete-but-aborted.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:657:        - \"Abort disposition vehicle: research §5b says the mapper carries stopReason through, but the seven intake kinds have no disposition field and turn_end's payload must be empty — resolved by carrying it on a trailing runtime_note (no new kind, per Anti-Shim) and updating the aborted corpus expected so the converter and the Story-3 fixture stay consistent.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:659:        - \"Failure-bucket mapping respects the closed ErrorCode union and the capture→lifecycle boundary rule: the converter returns a structured OpResult and index.ts (composition root) derives recordedGap from the code (invalid_event → gap recorded; otherwise health signal), since the capture surface may not import lifecycle/state.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:660:        - \"Confirmed PI per-step turn_end and agent_end carry content redundant with message_end, so the converter maps only message_end content and treats turn_end/agent_end as signals — avoiding double-capture.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:663:        - \"The declared MessageEndEvent slice does not surface a real PI entry id, so the converter synthesizes a per-session monotonic source-event index as the entry id. This is replay-stable when a reload/replay re-runs from the start (the AC-2.6 paths), but a reload that re-delivers only a suffix of history would misalign the synthesized index; the content-fingerprint last-resort tier collides only on identical content at the same block. Both are documented limitations until PI's real entry/response ids are wired into the higher key tiers.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:666:      - \"When PI's real entry id / provider response id are exposed on the message_end hook, they should replace the converter's synthesized source-event index in the idempotency key (they slot into the existing higher-precedence tiers). Until then the synthesized index is the entry id.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:670:      - \"(2) the map→accumulate orchestration lives in the index.ts composition root which calls converter.capture() for the batch+isolate step — forced by the check-boundaries rule that the capture surface may not import lifecycle (the accumulator and source-event counter are per-session state held in the connector closure); converter.capture()'s spec'd signature is unchanged;\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:748:          concern: \"Existing-thread resume/reload can silently skip new finalized events (verifier 004, critical). On resume/reload of an existing thread, newly finalized PI message_end events may be dropped from capture — a silent capture gap.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:778:    concern: \"Existing-thread resume/reload can silently skip new finalized events (verifier 004, critical). On resume/reload of an existing thread, newly finalized PI message_end events may be dropped from capture — a silent capture gap.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
