oard/02-domain-design.md:122:The domain maps the thread id to its file through the threads domain, then writes the batch to the thread's database in one coherent write flow. For each event it assigns the next position in the thread's order and records the source event. For events that produce readable conversation activity, it calls the `messages` surface to create messages and blocks. For events that affect turn state, it calls the `turns` surface to apply the open or close rule. It returns a result describing what happened to each event.\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:19:  | \"message_end\"\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36:export interface MessageEndEvent {\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:37:  entryId?: string;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:38:  position?: number;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:55:  position?: number;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:61:  position?: number;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:64:  entryId: string;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:65:  position?: number;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:82:  message_end: MessageEndEvent;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:181:  /** Composite, stable across tool_execution_start → tool_result → message_end\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:52:- Dispositions:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:70:- Dispositions: none (no findings)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:85:- Dispositions:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:102:- Dispositions:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:116:- Dispositions: none (no findings)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:129:- Dispositions: none (no findings)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:178:- Acceptance never delegated: run story gate myself, write receipt (implementor evidence, verifier evidence, gate result, dispositions, risks, baseli