-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:409:6. Drain report shape and the CLI rendering of dispositions.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:436:### Story 3: Turn Composition and Chunk Formation\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:438:**Governing idea:** Composition consumes message-level forms and degrades gracefully where they are missing; chunk boundaries are deterministic and final.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:26:- **AC-5.3**: The peek-ahead stop: a turn is evicted only if the zone's sum after evicting it remains ≥ target. The advance lands in [target, target + one turn) only when that landing is achievable without violating newest-closed-turn protection or the structural protection of trailing turnless singleton groups positioned after the newest closed turn; when those protections would otherwise have to be broken to reach the window, they take precedence and the zone lawfully stays above [target, target + one turn). The newest closed turn is never evicted.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:117:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:143:  boundary position = highest source_event_order in last evicted group\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:44:    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\"read both files\")));\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:45:    await connector.handlers.message_end(\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:57:    await connector.handlers.message_end(ctx, makeMessageEnd(makeToolResult({ id: \"call_b\", content: \"b body\" })));\npa